      "id": "https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ancient-hon-chuong-cham-tower",
      "url": "https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ancient-hon-chuong-cham-tower",
      "title": "[Atlas Obscura] Ancient Hon Chuong Cham Tower in De Gi, Vietnam",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://img.atlasobscura.com/sH0PdhoMoEi8HVced6ErW-fkdstuD_gPs9Dp14ImK2k/rt:fit/w:600/c:900:600:nowe:0:157/q:81/sm:1/scp:1/ar:1/aHR0cHM6Ly9hdGxh/cy1kZXYuczMuYW1h/em9uYXdzLmNvbS91/cGxvYWRzL3BsYWNl/X2ltYWdlcy9kZmY1/YjI4Zi0yYzI2LTRk/NzctOWRmMi1lNmQ5/NzIyYTQ3ODRjZTlm/ZGJkMmVmNjQ4MmRj/ODZfSU1HLTIwMjYw/ODMxLVdBMDAxNC5q/cGc.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p><img alt=\"\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://img.atlasobscura.com/Ueb-fLOeKOf-gZ6dF2dYraU4yyn2ZzqYAKCuyyvKOoI/rs:fill:300:200:1/g:ce/c:900:600:nowe:0:157/q:81/sm:1/scp:1/ar:1/aHR0cHM6Ly9hdGxh/cy1kZXYuczMuYW1h/em9uYXdzLmNvbS91/cGxvYWRzL3BsYWNl/X2ltYWdlcy9kZmY1/YjI4Zi0yYzI2LTRk/NzctOWRmMi1lNmQ5/NzIyYTQ3ODRjZTlm/ZGJkMmVmNjQ4MmRj/ODZfSU1HLTIwMjYw/ODMxLVdBMDAxNC5q/cGc.jpg\" width=\"300\"/></p> <p>Deep within the rugged heights of De Gi in Phu Cat lies one of the most obscure and isolated ancient architectural puzzles in Vietnam. Hon Chuong Tower is a tiny, solitary Cham ruin standing defiantly atop a massive rocky outcrop at an altitude of 779 meters.</p>\n<p>Both its exact chronology and original purpose remain shrouded in unanswered questions, adding to its deep aura of mystery. Its distinct, compact architecture and extreme isolation make it a genuinely thrilling destination for intrepid explorers.</p>\n<p>The high altitude climate offers breathtaking, sweeping vistas of majestic mountain landscapes and surrounding wilderness. Because very few travelers ever reach this remote summit, the site delivers a raw and authentic expedition into forgotten history.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-02T14:00:00+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Atlas Obscura",
          "url": "https://www.atlasobscura.com"
        }
      ],
